  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 882111,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "A issue was identified in the PDF export path for disclosed reports. When a report was exported to PDF, the export pipeline did not apply the same visibility and authorization scoping that governs the normal report view. As a result, the generated PDF could potentially include timeline content beyond what the requester was authorized to see, such as internal team activity, triage guidance, and internal fields, and reports at a limited disclosure level could potentially be rendered as if fully disclosed.\n\nThe root cause was that PDF generation assembled report content from the underlying timeline without re-checking each activity against the requester's permission level, effectively bypassing authorization for that code path rather than the report as a whole.\n\nThe issue was validated by our team and fixed promptly by enforcing the same per-activity visibility checks and disclosure-level scoping along the export path, as already applied elsewhere. We have found no evidence of misuse in our investigation to date, and no action is required from users.",
